{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/21621-what-do-we-know-about-the-lost-guild","id":21621,"title":"What do we know about the lost guild","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T07:47:34-08:00","id":21621,"title":"What do we know about the lost guild","content":"So we got a preview of the Mummy focused conspiracy. It's a great conspiracy but it has a terrible flaw. It's different to what I would have done <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> So what I really don't need is a forth project. That would be a Hunter Conspiracy designed to be the thematic opposites of the unrisen. Young instead of old. Empire builders instead of the remains of a fallen empire. Diplomatic and believers in human rights rather than bronze age tyrants. <br /> <br /> <br /> That to me says they're part of the European Union: Where formally hostile governments are now voluntarily surrendering their powers to a super-national body. The Arisen say there's nothing new under the sun, well they're wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm seeing a French gentleman's club that's become very popular with EU politicians; but long before then it was a popular gentleman's occult society that got hold of Napolian's discoveries in Egypt. Not just the Rosetta stone, but enough Iremite artifacts to create Relics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To complete the idea of complete opposites I was thinking that their Relics should be based on the lost sixth guild. So I turn to you, the people who know more about Mummy than me, what did the sixth guild do and what were their Relics like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T13:22:43-08:00","id":22546,"title":"","content":"The Sixth (or Lost) Guild were Artists (at least this is hinted at in the Guildhalls book). <br /> <br /> They had access to a unique magic called Ren-Heku, which was all to do with names. Particularly I believe &quot;true names&quot;. Its implied to be the most powerful form of Iremian magic. It remains a mystery if its an entirely different set of abilities from the traditional Mummy powers of Affinities and Utterances or if its simple a specialized sub-set of these abilities. <br /> <br /> So far we do not know if they even have access to relics or not. In Guildhall's its talked about in the Alchemists chapter that the Sixth Guild was the only one that did not require some base physical component from the Alchemists to do their trade/work. So its possible that the Deceived don't have &quot;guild relics&quot;. Likewise the extent to which they can/do interact with relics is a mystery.<br /> <br /> They are implied to have some link to Apotheosis, though exactly what connection they have to that mystical/enlightened state remains vague. Likewise, its implied the reason that so many Arisen don't believe they exist anymore is that claiming ones name makes a being immune to any magical scrutiny (so they can't be spied on/located/proved to exist my mystical means). <br /> <br /> They are Deathless, like the Arisen, but I do not believe they were created by the Rite of Return, as their Guild was purged before the Rite was conducted. Its implied that they were a &quot;sacrifice&quot; that was necessary for the Shan'Iatu to make their Empire &quot;Nameless&quot; (and therefore everlasting). <br /> <br /> They are roughly the equivalent of a Balial's Brood Vampire compared to a traditional Kindred. However, the differences are larger and more pronounced.<br /> <br /> To quote CAS in reference to this point: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/2105-so-how-is-deceived-coming-along?p=6658#post6658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, guys.<br /> <br /> As to <i>Book of the Deceived</i>, that's in-progress now and I'm pretty thrilled with how it's shaping up. As others mentioned, it's effectively the <i>Belial's Brood </i>of this line, and so I wanted to take a similarly direct hand in its development, which means I'm also one of the writing team this time around (whereas I will <b>not</b> be writing much on the next three sourcebooks for the line).<br /> <br /> Look for a Lost Guild teaser on the Mummy page/blog later in the month, but I'll tease one thing here by answering Hawthorn's question straight up: Yep, the Deceived are analogous to the Brood on <i>that</i> axis, as well. Unlike the Shuankhsen, they are technically Deathless (not Lifeless), and therefore operate under similar base assumptions as the Arisen. That said, they're a fundamentally different breed of Deathless being, and as such, expect to see a larger difference, mechanically speaking, between them and the Arisen than there was between Brood vampires and those of other covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they are being described as &quot;dark reflections&quot; of the Arisen by the books blurb on the Onyx Path site and that they will be possible player characters, I suspect they will be more sympathetic/sane then the Shuankhsen. <br /> <br /> On a final point, its very heavily implied that they now the &quot;Truth&quot; about what the Shan'Iatu were up to in Irem and may even know what their deal with Ammut was all about. Likewise, with what the Judges actually are. <br /> <br /> That's everything I think. Its all pretty vague and the stuff in the core reads like its written from an Arisen's point of view (which is to say it's a gross/bias oversimplification without understanding all the facts of the Deceived's true nature).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:12:34-08:00","id":22582,"title":"","content":"Thanks. It's a pity there's no hints to how their magic might have worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T19:43:20-08:00","id":22832,"title":"","content":"Its also implied , that they all posess, without exception, the Name-Decree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T20:53:48-08:00","id":24875,"title":"","content":"Or rather, that the Name-Decreed ones would be the only ones who survived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}